THOUGHT: NullAway still thinks `camera` is nullable at the `currentShader.begin(camera, context)` call. A common pattern to satisfy it is to copy the nullable field into a local variable after a null-check; the local can be treated as non-null. I’ll modify `flush()` to check `camera`, assign it to a local `Camera cam = camera;`, and then use `cam` in `sorter.sort` and `currentShader.begin`. This should eliminate the PASS_NULLABLE error without changing behavior. Then I’ll re-run the compile to confirm the error count drops by one.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '272,287c\	  public void flush() {
	    if (camera == null) return;
	    final Camera cam = camera;
	    sorter.sort(cam, renderables);
	    Shader currentShader = null;
	    for (int i = 0; i < renderables.size; i++) {
	      final Renderable renderable = renderables.get(i);
	      if (currentShader != renderable.shader) {
	        if (currentShader != null) currentShader.end();
	        currentShader = renderable.shader;
	        currentShader.begin(cam, context);
	      }
	      currentShader.render(renderable);
	    }
	    if (currentShader != null) currentShader.end();
	    renderablesPool.flush();
	    renderables.clear();
	  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g3d/ModelBatch.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "ModelBatch.java" -n new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

